module       version  words  summary
core         1.3         85  arithmetic, functions, logic, the stack, words and the session
decimal      1.0          7  decimal numbers for money: number mode, conversions, rounding
finance      1.0         33  time value of money, cash flows, depreciation, bonds, day counts
complex      1.0          7  complex numbers: parts, argument, conjugate, construction
special      1.0          7  gamma, beta and the standard normal distribution
matrices     1.0         38  linear algebra, matrix construction and reduction, polynomials
numerics     1.0         12  integration, roots, minima, derivatives and sums over any word
strings      1.0          7  string construction and manipulation
registers    1.0          7  64 storage registers of any type
dates        1.1         22  calendar arithmetic, workdays and holidays, time zones, sunrise and sunset
programs     1.0          1  HP-41 style programs with labels, jumps and subroutines

[1mdet[0m   A -- det(A)   [module matrices, Matrices]
    determinant of a square real or complex matrix
    takes 1 item (the last one named is on top):
      A          a matrix (real or complex)
    leaves 1 item:
      det(A)     
    example:  [2 2 $ 4 7 2 6] det
    which leaves:
[0] ℝ : 10.000000
    see also: tran ' minv pinv eig chol svd kron dim reshape get_aij set_aij 
              split_mat diag to_diag eye ones zeroes rand randn rrange join_v join_h cumsum_r 
              cumsum_c cmean rmean csum rsum cvar rvar cmin rmin cmax rmax 


[1mintegrate[0m   a b xt -- I   [module numerics, Numerics]
    integral of f over [a,b] (tanh-sinh with adaptive bisection; handles endpoint singularities)
    takes 3 items (the last one named is on top):
      a          a real number
      b          a real number
      xt         an execution token: @word or @command (see the numerics module)
    leaves 1 item:
      I          a matrix
    example:  0 pi @sin integrate
    see also: exec romberg fzero solve minimize deriv fsum fprod tol nevals interr 

{}
[exit 0]
